From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cuttlely vendor <vendor@cuttlely.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuttlely: probe cache fd lifecycle

What: count SQLite header-probe owners by device/inode across every state database connection owner (SessionDB writers, pooled readers, ledger, maintenance, repair, backup and doctor helpers) and close probe descriptors once the last owner of that inode has closed its SQLite connection. Replaced path generations are fenced by inode and their probes close when unowned; unowned probes are transient. Why: the probe cache kept raw descriptors for the process lifetime and retired descriptors without closing them, so temporary-profile churn leaked one descriptor per profile until EMFILE (cuttlely#536). Closing only after the last SQLite owner closes keeps POSIX advisory-lock guarantees for peer connections.
---
